{"name":"Galliano","hex":"#d8a723","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Galliano","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Liquore Galliano L'Autentico, a bright yellow Italian liqueur flavoured with herbs, star anise and vanilla, and used in several cocktails including Harvey Wallbanger"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Galliano"}],"entries":[{"title":"Galliano (liqueur)","blocks":[{"text":"Liquore Galliano L'Autentico, known more commonly as Galliano, is a brand of sweet herbal liqueur produced in Italy. It was created in 1896 by Tuscan distiller and brandy producer Arturo Vaccari and named after Giuseppe Galliano, an Italian officer of the Royal Italian Army of the First Italo-Ethiopian War."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Galliano-and-glass.jpg/330px-Galliano-and-glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galliano_(liqueur)","wikidata":"Q1331962"},{"title":"Galliano (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Galliano is an Italian surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Cecilia Galliano, Argentine actress, model, and TV presenter","Giuseppe Galliano (1846–1896), Italian army officer","John Galliano, British fashion designer","Richard Galliano, French accordion player"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galliano_(surname)","wikidata":"Q20996239"},{"title":"Galliano (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Galliano are a London-based acid jazz group that were originally active between 1988 and 1997. Galliano was the first to record on Eddie Piller and Gilles Peterson's Acid Jazz record label, then the first signing to Peterson's newly formed Talkin' Loud label. Original member Robert Gallagher was joined by Constantine Weir (vocals), and Crispin Robinson (percussion) that would perform Last Poets-influenced spoken-word pieces. Michael Snaith joined as the trio became a band in order to tour their first album on Talkin' Loud, In Pursuit of the 13th Note. The album featured Roy Ayers, and was awarded an Edison Populair writing award in 1992."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/SBE25.jpg/330px-SBE25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galliano_(band)","wikidata":"Q286110"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Mus%C3%A9e_de_la_Gourmandise_%E2%80%93_Mission_Gourmande_%E2%80%93_Salle_2_%280013%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Mus%C3%A9e_de_la_Gourmandise_%E2%80%93_Mission_Gourmande_%E2%80%93_Salle_2_%280013%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Mus%C3%A9e_de_la_Gourmandise_%E2%80%93_Mission_Gourmande_%E2%80%93_Salle_2_%280013%29.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Mus%C3%A9e_de_la_Gourmandise_%E2%80%93_Mission_Gourmande_%E2%80%93_Salle_2_%280013%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Mus%C3%A9e_de_la_Gourmandise_%E2%80%93_Mission_Gourmande_%E2%80%93_Salle_2_%280013%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Mus%C3%A9e_de_la_Gourmandise_%E2%80%93_Mission_Gourmande_%E2%80%93_Salle_2_%280013%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Advertising statuette for the Galliano brand.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMus%C3%A9e_de_la_Gourmandise_%E2%80%93_Mission_Gourmande_%E2%80%93_Salle_2_(0013).tif"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Galliano-sign","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Galliano-sign.jpg/500px-Galliano-sign.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galliano-sign.jpg","share":0.486875},{"title":"Yellow Color","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Yellow_Color.jpg/500px-Yellow_Color.jpg","ratio":1.333333